            "why": "Palomar accepts a Mathlib revision only if it is an ancestor of mathlib4 master, and its Challenge renderer runs `lake exe cache get-` inside a no-network sandbox. Mathlib's cache tool on the v4.29.x line calls getProofWidgets from getFiles, which fetches the ProofWidgets cloud release from github.com, so cache discovery exits 1 and every render check fails at the workspace stage before a Challenge is read. mathlib4 PR #37290 removed that call, merged 2026-03-30 as b301d257a1c13bc4e27350c06e5169b8b08a53ed, which is on master, seven commits ahead of the v4.29.0 tag, and still declares leanprover/lean4:v4.29.0 in its own lean-toolchain. The release pins that commit and the dependency revisions from its own lake-manifest.json; the accepted toolchain does not move and the private project keeps its own pin and cache untouched. Diagnosis: docs/formal_math/palomar/palomar_renderability_diagnosis_2026_09_02.md."
          },
          "directory_name": "plectis-erdos-lean",
          "display_name": "Plectis Erd\u0151s Lean",
          "programme": {
            "name": "the Plectis programme",
            "note": "The papers behind each entry, the eight problem pages and the further verified work outside this release are indexed at <https://wcook04.github.io/plectis/maths/>. The reviewed claim registry, the declaration atlas and the papers live in the companion public corpus <https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-lean-erdos249-257>; this repository is its Comparator and Palomar projection at one commit, and entry counts here never compose with declaration counts there.",
            "url": "https://wcook04.github.io/plectis/"
